a }_{2}=-5.$ \n\nSince $A$ is not a scalar matrix, we conclude that $A$ is not diagonalizable, and its Jordan canonical form is\n\n$$\nJ={J}_{2}(-5)=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112477/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b629bead-e64a-5e73-ae42-80d4ebb3762b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112477"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection/e7848fe7db7a6e6302dd1b677c2f368d728d634331fb123a9bc885369d87d5df" :answer/id #uuid "83e96c1a-ebae-5656-a09b-02462f524c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection/6c20aa809075840d2583d3881bc9eb0fabfff6b10c5859c1e93e9f46e326c94e" :answer/id #uuid "d47c5843-17c5-532e-8d63-344c6b076de8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection/9e02ac843816750d483fa24d0bcae89d715456cc4932772f1422cbab38002b73" :answer/id #uuid "db6f153c-5e38-5f8d-bd42-8938b36f96d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection/e7a040f53a0718aae8e6e8dc532082b771517e052c716f867a1517a8f876732c" :answer/id #uuid "ecdfb274-f496-5caa-b48c-e5a39018b71f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection/6434096b15c030b32afe93a5640dee16c6842e1898343cd7ad452d2c2954486a" :answer/id #uuid "9be8aa47-6155-54c6-9a7d-53eeda148e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-109095/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "241546c4-0f61-5343-bfcf-78835c112df8" :answer-field/key "selection" 